A||||5||aubicon||temp switch||||1||
Z||000000||aubicon||09-07-2001||11:33 PM||||i just refilled the cooling system in my 87 gt, i ran the engine till it overheated, the fan never came on. i think it is the temp switch but i have no idia where it is located. there are two sensors on the front of the engine and one on the back. any idias which one is the switch? any other idias to why the fan will not come on would also be appreciated.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Leadfoot||09-07-2001||11:40 PM||||It sounds like the switch.  It is located near the coolant fill near the back right of the decklid and is screwed into the intake manifold.  You can check to see if the fan works by jumpering the plug.  <P>Also the fan should kick on when you turn on the a/c.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Leadfoot (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Rodney||09-08-2001||09:53 AM||||The fan switch has a green wire with a gray tracer on it. Pull the connector off by squeezing the wide sides. Ground the wire and turn the key to the run position. The fan should run. If not it could be the switch, fan, relay or bad wire somewhere. Maybe a corroded connection somewhere also. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||aubicon||09-08-2001||07:03 PM||||i ran diagnostics and it said that nothing was wrong could it still be the temp switch or would it be somewhere else in the circuit, i will go try the jumper trick now.||||reg||1
Z||000004||maryjane||09-08-2001||07:34 PM||||I may be wrong here but I think the code diagnostics at alcl will only show problems associated with the temp sensor feeding the ecm it's info. code 14 or 15. I don't think a bad cooling fan temp switch will set a code.||||reg||1
Z||000005||sqoach||09-08-2001||08:09 PM||||Yes, turn on your A/C to see if the fan kicks on. If not, it's most likely that you either have a bad relay, or fan motor. If it does kick on, it is probably the fan switch.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">        <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||1
